## #736 — `/bg list` growing elapsed time → **commented + closed**

Genuinely fixed in 689cd3bd. Verified before claiming it:
• Three writers stamp the runtime, not the two the issue predicted — the spawn-failure early return in run_background_command stores finished and returns before the wait path. All three route through one shared stamp_runtime helper.
• The abstention case turned out to be reachable, not theoretical: finished is a Relaxed store, so a reader can see the flag before the mutex-guarded stamp. elapsed_column prints -- rather than borrowing the live clock.
• 51 `commands_bg` tests pass. The regression test freezes elapsed across a real 400ms sleep — the weaker "elapsed is small" assertion passes on the buggy code, which is why this survived.

